  "componentConditions": {
    "tx_nd_veterans_reemployment-petition-2": "Used only where the court requires a petition or did not hold the hearing. Gov't Code § 411.0729 names no filing party and imposes no petition requirement: the court holds a hearing and, unless it finds issuance is not in the best interest of justice, enters the order. OCA publishes a model petition because in practice some courts require one. Try the no-filing route first.",
    "tx_nd_veterans_reemployment-proposed-order-3": "Filed with the petition on the petition route. OCA instructions state that in most courts a proposed order must be submitted with the petition.",
    "tx_nd_veterans_reemployment-fee-waiver-statement-4": "Used only where there is a filing at all AND the participant cannot afford the fees and costs. No fee arises on the no-filing route. Tex. R. Civ. P. 145 requires the clerk to make this form available without charge or request in any event."
  },
